    "result_text": "All tests pass. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the salutation feature: the request may include `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the response returns `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, falling back to just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`Owner.java` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `title` field (with getter/setter) and a `@Transient getSalutation()` deriving `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when `title` is null/blank. This follows the existing pattern of derived getters (`getAgeBand()`, `getContactPreference()`, etc.).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (string) to the `OwnerFields` request schema and `salutation` (readOnly) to the `Owner` response schema. The generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` and MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` auto-map `title` (request\u2192entity) and both `title`/`salutation` (entity\u2192response) by name \u2014 no mapper edits needed, mirroring the other derived fields.\n\n3. **`ApplyOwner.java`** \u2014 copies `title` onto the entity so the `PUT /owners/{ownerId}` endpoint handles it too, for consistency.\n\n4. **Database schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 appended a `title VARCHAR(10)` column at the end of the `owners` table, matching the established \"append new columns at the end\" convention (as `address_line1`/`address_line2` were). Since the test profile is **hsqldb** and its `data.sql` uses positional inserts, I also appended a trailing `NULL` to each seed owner row so the column counts match.\n\nVerification: `./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` (which asserts `$.salutation` == `\"DR who\"`) passes, and it's the only test class in the suite.",
